@flexiarg operator/report-the-act-done
@title Report the Act Done
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-JSYCf5 turn-Wj27g4; first proposed for: The operator performs an operational act outside the session (transferred a repo, changed a setting) that changes the world the agent is reasoning about.
@why [orchestration/state-in-substrate-deltas-in-messages]

! conclusion: open with a one-clause report of the completed act, then act on its consequences in the same turn.

  + IF:
    the act changes state the agent's current or next work depends on.

  + HOWEVER:
    the agent cannot see out-of-session acts; an unreported change leaves it reasoning against a stale world, but a long report wastes the turn.

  + THEN:
    open with a one-clause report of the completed act, then act on its consequences in the same turn.

  + BECAUSE:
    That pattern keeps world state in the substrate and messages as deltas; the operator's report is the human-side instance — a state delta carried in a message so the agent's model re-syncs.
